{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/708303-vampire-the-second-city-game-near-minneapolis-mn","id":708303,"title":"Vampire the Second City game near Minneapolis, MN","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-19T00:11:49-07:00","id":708303,"title":"Vampire the Second City game near Minneapolis, MN","content":"Looking for gamers for a new table top game starting in Nov.<br /> <br /> We meet every Friday. We have a regular group of three that meets every Friday except for eight weeks out of the year. Our group gets together at Fantasy Flight in Roseville.<br /> <br /> The game will allow characters to create up to 4th gen vampires. Vampires will start at 7th generation.<br /> <br /> Feel free to write up a background. Writing a background = more dots at character creation.<br /> <br /> How do you write a background for a Second City Vampire game? Great question.<br /> <br /> Here are two timelines you can use to understand the age we'll be playing in.<br /> <br /> Bibical: The Flood just happened. Genesis 6:11-7:24<br /> <br /> History: ~8000 BCE.<br /> <br /> The more work you put into a background the more benefits.<br /> <br /> Simple background: Name and what has happened to your character.<br /> <br /> Moderate background: Same as simple with more depth. How your character survived, others they met, how they handle the new world, etc.<br /> <br /> Complex background. Same as moderate with genuine development. A tale of the trials and tribulations your character has endured.<br /> <br /> I prefer a lot of angst for characters. Days of inactivity are not nearly as profound and compelling as the days where one's tested. We learn from failure, not from success. Learning is painful, hence why we tend not to repeat acts that caused us pain compared to those that did not.<br /> <br /> Feel free to email me any possible character ideas, gross or subtle. We can discuss them at great length before character creation in Nov.<br /> <br /> Clans:<br /> <br /> Assamite<br /> Cappadocian<br /> Followers of Set<br /> Gangrel<br /> Lasombra<br /> Malkavian<br /> Nosferatu<br /> Ravnos<br /> Salubri<br /> Toreador<br /> True Brujah<br /> Tzimisce<br /> Ventrue<br /> <br /> The first story is going to be extremely episodic. There'll be a lot of individual plots running with very little character-to-character interaction. Most characters will go through the entire story without encountering another player character. My goal of first story is a place where the characters can find themselves and motives before meeting other group members. This going to be a great story with plenty of action and very little downtime.<br /> <br /> Reminder: this Vampire game is before history. Verbal language is just forming. High fantasy abounds. Power is rampant. Take any preconceived notions of Vampire games and throw them out the window. The Jyhad isn't a thought.<br /> <br /> Please feel free to ask any questions.<br /> <br /> Thanks","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8692-childe-of-arbenghast","name":"childe of ArbenGhast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}